From 44fa9b6aef69cecb7ee95b85321be94044651976 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:07:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] voice: bridge the remote microphone into PipeWire

The remote carries a microphone but sends nothing until the host sends
the vendor command F9 03 as a two-byte SET_REPORT on the feature report,
after which it emits 124-byte reports at 66.7 per second, each holding
two 60-byte HFP wideband blocks: an H2 header and a 57-byte mSBC frame.
That is a live 15 ms stream, so it belongs in an audio graph rather than
in a file.

Add a small daemon that reads the remote's hidraw node, arms and re-arms
the stream, decodes the frames with libsbc and publishes a PipeWire
source of S16LE mono at 16 kHz. Decoding in userspace keeps mSBC out of
the kernel, where there is no format to carry it and no decoder to use.

The microphone button alone does not start the stream on real hardware
either, so arming is a host policy: by default while the button is held
plus a tail, optionally whenever a client records or unconditionally.
The remote stops on its own after about six seconds, which the restart
opcode every 4 s prevents, and a second without audio is treated as the
stream having died.

The button is read as KEY_VOICECOMMAND from the input device the kernel
module registers, so the report layout is decoded in one place. The
remote drops the link when idle and reconnects on the next key press,
so the daemon runs for the whole session: it waits on udev for a remote
bound to lgmagic and attaches once its hidraw and evdev nodes are both
accessible.

The udev rule gives the seat owner access to those two nodes, which the
daemon needs and which are otherwise root-only.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 .gitignore                   |   3 +
 52-lgmagic-hidraw.rules      |   4 +
 voice/Makefile               |  29 ++
 voice/lg-magic-voice.service |  12 +
 voice/lg_magic_voice.c       | 928 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 976 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 52-lgmagic-hidraw.rules
 create mode 100644 voice/Makefile
 create mode 100644 voice/lg-magic-voice.service
 create mode 100644 voice/lg_magic_voice.c

--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -19,3 +19,6 @@ __pycache__/
 
 # Host-side tests
 tests/test_airmouse_math
